From 2da31e5257041dc8f0cc5d93c4666292357e0336 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 04:12:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(policy): save the audit trail in a versioned,
 append-friendly file format

Tenth slice: a DENY that is forgotten when the process dies is not an audit
trail. The in-memory log stays the source of truth while the app runs;
core/policy/PolicyAuditFile is only the format storage writes at the end of a
session and reads at the start of the next one.

```
andcode-audit 1
1700000000000|agent:write_file|MEDIUM|REQUIRE_APPROVAL|OUTSIDE_WORKSPACE|write ../secrets/A.kt
```

- Versioned and line-based: a file the app does not understand is refused
  (EMPTY / BAD_HEADER / UNSUPPORTED_VERSION / TOO_LARGE) rather than read
  wrongly, and an unknown level, decision or reason code is not guessed at.
- Append friendly: encodeLine writes one record, so storage can append instead
  of rewriting; encode writes the header plus the newest MAX_ENTRIES.
- A torn last line is counted, not fatal: the app appends while it runs, so a
  crash can leave half a line; Decoded.skippedLines reports the damage instead
  of making the whole trail unreadable.
- No secrets on disk: only actor, level, decision, codes and the redacted
  summary are stored, and SecretRedaction runs again on read because a
  hand-edited file can carry anything.
- InMemoryPolicyAuditLog.exportText()/restore() move the trail through the
  format. A rejected file, or one with nothing readable in it, leaves the
  in-memory trail untouched - losing live decisions to a torn stored copy would
  be the worst of both.
- Bounded: 256 KiB and 500 entries, so a long-lived file cannot grow forever.

Tests: PolicyAuditFileTest (22).
