+## The saved trail
+
+`PolicyAuditFile` is the part of "an audit trail" that has to outlive the process, kept separate from the
+log so that `record()` never does IO.
+
+```
+andcode-audit 1
+1700000000000|agent:write_file|MEDIUM|REQUIRE_APPROVAL|OUTSIDE_WORKSPACE|write ../secrets/A.kt
+```
+
+- **Versioned and line-based.** A file the app does not understand is refused (`BAD_HEADER`,
+  `UNSUPPORTED_VERSION`, `TOO_LARGE`, `EMPTY`) instead of being read wrongly.
+- **Append friendly**: `encodeLine` writes one record, so storage can append; `encode` writes the header
+  and the newest `MAX_ENTRIES` (500).
+- **A torn line is counted, not fatal**: the app appends while running, so a crash can leave half a line;
+  `Decoded.skippedLines` reports how many were dropped rather than making the rest unreadable.
+- **No raw commands**: only the actor, level, decision, reason codes and the redacted summary are stored,
+  and `SecretRedaction` runs again on read, because a hand-edited file can contain anything.
+- **Nothing is lost on a bad restore**: `InMemoryPolicyAuditLog.restore` leaves the in-memory trail alone
+  when the file is rejected or nothing in it could be read.
 
